    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 10 October 2005, the erection of a single-storey detached outbuilding measuring a depth of 5m, a width of 6.45m and a ridge height of 3.65m reducing to 2.7m at the eaves was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because it is located more than 5 metres from the house and takes up less than 50 percent of the rear garden.\r\n"
